        <figcaption class="cartel"><span class="no">No. 1</span><span><i>Moby-Dick</i>, Herman Melville · ch. 1</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="piece skied desk-only" data-a style="--area:b">
        <div class="mount text"><blockquote>A thing of beauty is a joy for ever:<br>Its loveliness increases; it will never<br>Pass into nothingness</blockquote></div>
        <figcaption class="cartel"><span class="no">No. 2</span><span><i>Endymion</i>, John Keats · book I, lines 1–3</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="piece skied" data-a style="--area:c" data-words="statistics reading days books passages">
        <div class="mount stat dark">
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Passages</dt><dd>115</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Books</dt><dd>6</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Days</dt><dd>63</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Best run</dt><dd>4d</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="cartel"><span class="no">No. 3</span><span>From the Statistics page</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="piece skied" data-a style="--area:d">
        <div class="mount text small"><blockquote>You pierce my soul. I am half agony, half hope.</blockquote></div>
        <figcaption class="cartel"><span class="no">No. 4</span><span><i>Persuasion</i>, Jane Austen · ch. 23</span></figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="stack" style="grid-area:e">
      <figure class="piece wide">
        <div class="mount text">
          <blockquote>I went to the woods because I wished to live deliberately, to front only the essential facts of life, and see if I could not learn what it had to teach, and not, when I came to die, discover that I had not lived.</blockquote>
          <p class="note"><b>Your note</b>Read this again before deciding about the move.</p>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="cartel"><span class="no">No. 5</span><span><i>Walden</i>, Henry David Thoreau · ch. 2</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="piece desk-only">
        <div class="mount text small dark"><blockquote>The person, be it gentleman or lady, who has not pleasure in a good novel, must be intolerably stupid.</blockquote></div>
        <figcaption class="cartel"><span class="no">No. 5a</span><span><i>Northanger Abbey</i>, Jane Austen · ch. 14</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="lede-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">A library for your book highlights</p>
        <h1 id="title">Every line you kept, <em>hung where you can see it.</em></h1>
        <p class="sub">Leaflogue gathers the passages you highlighted on your e-reader and the notes you wrote beside them, keeps them on your own computer, and helps you find any of them again.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#download">Get the desktop beta <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/start/install/">Read the guide</a>
        </div>
        <p class="fine">Free and open source · No account · Linux, Mac &amp; Windows beta</p>
